  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 7580cd21).\n\n## What changed\n\nEdge and feature picks added to the selection on Ctrl. On macOS Control is the secondary (right) click, so a Mac user could not Ctrl+click to add an edge chain to an operation's picks, while the keyboard shortcuts already use the command modifier.\n\n- `interact::Mods.ctrl` is renamed to `Mods.command`. It is built from egui's `modifiers.command` (Cmd on macOS, Ctrl elsewhere) through a new `From<egui::Modifiers>` impl, which the shell now uses.\n- Pick add/toggle reads `mods.command`: `edge_pick::queue_edge_pick`, `interact::queue_boundary_pick` (boundary toggle), `feature_click::click` (feature add), and the `ui.input` conversion in `egui_app/shell.rs`.\n- Shift keeps its meaning exactly (add in feature modes, whole loop in Edge mode, close in boundary mode).\n- Windows/Linux: egui sets `command` whenever Ctrl is held, so behaviour is unchanged there.\n- UI hint strings are not touched (#1239).\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/1238-pick-command-modifier.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning test: `the_command_modifier_from_egui_toggles_and_control_alone_does_not` (crates/ui/tests/edge_loop_pick.rs). It converts `egui::Modifiers::COMMAND`, Shift and Control-alone, asserts Control alone does not add on macOS, and that the command modifier toggles an edge in.\n\nUpdated, still green: `command_click_toggles_one_edge_in_and_out` (was ctrl), and the boundary_picks CTRL constant is now CMD (`command: true`). Shift tests unchanged.\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test edge_loop_pick --test boundary_picks`: all pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: ok (ui lib, boundary, boundary_picks, edge_loop_pick, operations, theme_files).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No Mac was used. The macOS behaviour rests on egui's `command` mapping and the converted-`Modifiers` test; it was not run on hardware.\n- The feature-mode add path in `feature_click::click` is changed but has no direct test (the function is `pub(crate)`); it is covered only by the rename compiling and the existing suites staying green.\n\nChangelog: fix: edge and feature pick add-to-selection uses the platform command modifier (Cmd on macOS, Ctrl elsewhere); Control alone no longer adds on macOS (#1238)\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #1238\n",
